% voxel_mesh — cubes of side h filling a model (a part, a body, a loaded STL/OBJ or any closed triangle mesh)
%
% Usage:      v = voxel_mesh(model, h)
%             v = voxel_mesh(part(), 2)          the open part, 2 mm cubes
% Computes:   the voxel mesh: every cube of the grid whose centre is inside the closed surface (voxelize, the same
%             voxel.js PartCraft's Simulation and Generative workspaces use, so node and element numbers match
%             theirs). Prints the grid, the element count and the voxel volume against the model's own volume.
% Method:     voxelize(model, h); the model's volume by the divergence theorem over its triangles
%             (V = Σ (a · (b × c)) / 6, mesh_quality does the same for any closed triangle surface).
% Units:      the model's length unit (PartCraft parts: mm).
% Limits:     the surface must be closed; cubes follow curved faces in steps of h (volume error about the
%             surface area × h/4 in the worst case, much less on average); thin walls need h below half the wall.
% References: PartCraft voxel.js (cube centres tested by ray parity).
% Check:      box 100 × 10 × 10 at h = 2.5: 640 cubes, volume 10000 exactly; cylinder r 10, len 20 at h 0.5:
%             volume within 1 % of πr²len (bin/test-craftscript.mjs --lib).
function v = voxel_mesh(model, h)
v = voxelize(model, h);
info = meshInfo(v);
s = meshOf(model);
q = mesh_quality(s);
V = info.elements * info.h^3;
fprintf('voxel_mesh: %d × %d × %d grid of %g cubes, %d elements, volume %.6g (the surface encloses %.6g, %+.2f %%)\n', ...
  info.nx, info.ny, info.nz, info.h, info.elements, V, q.volume, 100 * (V / q.volume - 1));
end
